    description: ""  # 6b9e
    fields:  # 6b9e
      statement: "AnalysisRun.toolchain field is HARDCODED to {name: 'python', version: '3.12.3'} for ALL 84 runs, regardless of pass language. The bash analyzer, JS analyzer, Solidity analyzer — all report toolchain as 'python 3.12.3'. AnalysisRun.execution_id is unique per run (84 UUIDs for 84 runs), not per CLI invocation — so it cannot group passes that came from the same hypergumbo invocation"  # 6b9e
      root_cause: "(1) toolchain captures the HOST Python interpreter rather than the analysis tool. The bash analyzer's toolchain should record bash version or tree-sitter-bash grammar version; the JS analyzer should record its parser version. Current value is useless for cross-tool reproducibility. (2) execution_id is misnamed — it functions as a per-pass UUID identical in role to run_signature, not as a per-invocation group key. Schema-doc consumers would assume execution_id groups runs into invocations"  # 6b9e
